Revision history for pyModbusTCP

0.4.0a3 2026-xx-xx (alpha: the command line tools, their options and output, may still change before 0.4.0)

    Summary of the changes since 0.3.1 (0.4.0a1 and 0.4.0a2 included).

    Breaking changes:

    - server: DataBank and DataHandler are replaced by a data store (MemoryStore, server.store), see "Migrating
      from DataBank and DataHandler" in the server guide: on_*_change() callbacks -> store.subscribe(), virtual
      mode -> store.map(), ext_engine -> function handlers (@server.function), DataHandler.Return -> exceptions
      (IllegalDataAddress...), srv_info -> RequestContext.
    - server: secure defaults: idle_timeout (300 s), request_timeout (30 s), max_connections (64) and
      max_connections_per_host (16), None disables them. start() raises NetworkError if already running.
    - client/server: stricter argument checks (TypeError/ValueError instead of a silent conversion or truncation),
      numpy booleans are no longer accepted as coil values.
    - client: the function code of a reply must match the request (MB_RECV_ERR otherwise).
    - client (since 0.4.0a2): the arguments of ModbusClient after auto_close are keyword-only, no_delay is renamed
      tcp_no_delay (argument and property).
    - server: the typed shortcuts of the store (read_float32(), write_int32()...) take a byte_order (ByteOrder,
      default ABCD) instead of big_endian: big_endian=False is now ByteOrder.CDAB, BADC and DCBA are available.
      New shortcuts read/write_uint16() and read/write_int16() (1 register, no byte order), read/write_uint64() and
      read/write_int64(): one shortcut for each DataType.
    - examples: client_serial_gw.py and server_serial_gw.py are removed (replaced by the gateways of the tools).
    - server: the arguments of ModbusServer after no_block are keyword-only (only host, port and no_block are
      positional): ModbusServer('0.0.0.0', 5020, read_only=True).
    - server: allowed_hosts is a tuple of str (was a list), set a new value to change it: a change in place
      would be silently lost.
    - server/tools: an allow list entry with host bits set (like "192.168.1.5/24", often a typo for one address)
      is refused (ValueError, or exit status 2 for -A/--allow): write "192.168.1.0/24" or "192.168.1.5".

    New features:

    - server: transactions (every request is atomic, 0x17 included), access rules (ReadOnly, AccessControl,
      Guard), one store per unit id, read_only, allowed_hosts (None: every host, []: no host).
    - codec: Codec(DataType, ByteOrder) converts 16/32/64 bits integers and IEEE floats to registers and back, in
      the ABCD, CDAB, BADC or DCBA byte order, for the client and the server store (read_values/write_values).
      ByteOrder64 gives the 8 orders of a 64 bits value (like CDABGHEF), for a Codec only (rare devices).
    - client: context manager, TCP_NODELAY (tcp_no_delay), timeout for the whole request.
    - client: broadcast=True on the write functions (and custom_request()) sends the request to the unit id 0
      (broadcast of a TCP to RTU gateway) without waiting for a reply; a late reply of the gateway is ignored.
    - tools: mbtcp-tcp2rtu --allow-broadcast answers a broadcast at once with the normal response of its function
      (it was exception 0x0B after the timeout), then keeps the bus silent for --broadcast-delay (default 0.1 s);
      only the write functions can be broadcast (0x05, 0x06, 0x0F, 0x10, 0x15, 0x16). A few broadcasts can wait for
      the bus (--broadcast-buffer, default 4), the next ones get exception 0x06 at once; one that waited more than
      --broadcast-max-age (default 10 s) is dropped: a flood never builds a backlog of old writes.
    - client: broadcast_interval (default 0.15 s) spaces two broadcast requests: a loop can't flood a gateway.
    - client: connect_retries (default 0) and connect_retry_delay (default 0.5 s) retry a failed connect, with an
      exponential backoff and a jitter (open() and auto_open). A request is never sent twice.
    - client: auto_open reconnects for the current request if the server has closed the connection (idle timeout,
      restart): the request no longer fails, only the next one reconnected before. A request sent on a connection
      reset before the server read it is sent again once on a new connection.
    - client: is_open is False as soon as the server has closed or reset the connection (server stopped, idle
      timeout), no longer only after a failed request; the connection is then closed on the client side too.
    - tools: command line tools (python -m pyModbusTCP.tools, or the mbtcp-* commands of pyModbusTCP-cli with
      "pip install pyModbusTCP[cli]"): mbtcp-server, mbtcp-client (table output, csv/json, write-read, typed
      values with -T/-b), mbtcp-tcp2rtu and mbtcp-rtu2tcp gateways (with RS-485 mode, needs pyserial).
    - typing: type hints on the whole package (py.typed).
    - docs: Sphinx documentation rewritten (guides, tools, security, examples), SECURITY.md.

    Fixes:

    - client: many robustness fixes (timeouts, invalid replies, transaction ids, is_open, write replies check).
    - server: Modbus compliance (0x05, 0x0F, 0x10, 0x17, 0x2B/0x0E, MBAP length), malformed requests answered
      with an exception instead of closing the session, port hijacking on Windows (SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE).
    - tools: mbtcp-tcp2rtu fair queue by client host (denial of service), invalid function codes refused.
    - utils: valid_host() edge cases (empty host, NUL and non-ASCII chars).
    - server: read_only also refuses 0x15 (write file record) and 0x16 (mask write register), and a fallback
      handler only gets the read functions (0x01 to 0x04, 0x2B/0x0E): 0x08 or a private function could write.
    - server: allowed_hosts, read_only, max_connections, max_connections_per_host, request_timeout and idle_timeout
      are properties: a new value is checked like in the constructor and applies at once, also to a running server
      (a whitelist set after the constructor was silently ignored: every client was still accepted). A new
      allowed_hosts closes the sessions of the clients it no longer allows.
    - server: a handler that returns a PDU over 253 bytes gets a "slave device failure" (no oversized frame).
    - server: the change events of the threaded listeners wait in a bounded queue (MemoryStore.notify_queue_size,
      10000): a slow listener can't make the memory grow without limit, the events over it are dropped and logged.

    Build: pyproject.toml with hatchling, Python 3.10 to 3.14.

0.4.0a2 2026-10-17 (alpha)

    See 0.4.0a3.

0.4.0a1 2026-10-15 (alpha)

    See 0.4.0a3.

0.3.1 2026-09-29

    - fix ModbusServer: debug messages now include OSError exceptions produced by getpeername (thanks to Pär Åhlund).
    - fix ModbusClient: prevent incomplete frame transmission by using sendall (thanks to aamir-azeez).
    - updated compatibility test (python versions): remove 3.8/3.9, add 3.13/3.14.

0.3.0 2024-09-04

    - pyModbusTCP.client: now use the standard logging method as in the server part.
    - ModbusClient: debug flag is removed (see examples/client_debug.py).

0.2.2 2024-07-31

    - fix ModbusServer: wrong check of discrete inputs length in DataBank (thanks to OTnetproj).
    - updated compatibility test (python versions): remove 3.7, add 3.12.

0.2.1 2023-11-21

    - fix ModbusServer: wrong check of input registers length in DataBank (thanks to monsieurvor).
    - improve hostname validation in utils (thanks to MCXIV and schmocker).
    - experimental add of read_device_identification() (over modbus encapsulated interface) to client and server.
    - experimental add of write_read_multiple_registers() function (code 0x17) to client and server (thanks to tanj).
    - updated compatibility test (python versions): remove 3.5/3.6, add 3.11.

0.2.0 2022-06-05

    - ModbusClient: parameters are now properties instead of methods (more intuitive).
    - ModbusClient: now TCP auto open mode is active by default (auto_open=True, auto_close=False).
    - ModbusClient: add custom_request method for send user define PDU to modbus server.
    - ModbusClient: remove RTU mode.
    - ModbusClient: clarify some things (private methods and internal vars rename).
    - ModbusServer: big redesign to improve readability and maintainability.
    - ModbusServer: no longer use hard linked class DataBank (it now return a deprecation warn).
    - ModbusServer: add of ModbusServerDataHandler and DefaultDataBank class for easy customize.
    - add or update server examples for new modbus server design.
    - some updates on tests, fix random arrays generation on client test part.
    - clarify usage of root privilege for open tcp/502 (avoid Errno 13) in server example.
    - python 2 end of support.

0.1.10 2021-03-02

    - word_list_to_long() and long_list_to_word(), now support 64 bits long long with opt long_long.
    - encode_ieee() and decode_ieee(), now support double-precision format with opt double.
    - add shortcut alias for functions with long names in utils.
    - rewrite of some functions in utils.
    - improve test_utils readability.
    - server DataBank enforce type check on set data methods to avoid server crash (thanks to xuantw).
    - now get_2comp can deal with negative python int.
    - remove reference to devel github branch.
    - improve last_error_txt() and last_except_txt().

0.1.9 2021-02-26

    - add module error MB_SOCK_CLOSE_ERR (occur if frame send on close socket).
    - add modbus exception EXP_NEGATIVE_ACKNOWLEDGE (code 0x07) to constants.
    - add last_error_txt() and last_except_txt() for produce human readable status.
    - add EXP_TXT, EXP_DETAILS and MB_ERR_TXT dicts to constants (text representation of codes).
    - update of the compatibility test for python version: remove 2.6/3.2/3.3, add 3.7/3.8/3.9.
    - conform to PEP 396 (add pyModbusTCP.__version__ field).

0.1.8 2018-10-15

    - fix ModbusServer: avoid hard coded TCP port (thanks to akobyl).
    - add stop() and is_run property to ModbusServer (thanks to Rugiewitz).

0.1.7 2018-08-20

    - fix ModbusServer issue on Windows (thanks to andreascian).

0.1.6 2018-05-14

    - fix multiple TCP packets recv issue in ModbusClient and ModbusServer (thanks Farin94).

0.1.5 2017-11-23

    - add long_list_to_word to utils.
    - add float support as example.

0.1.4 2017-11-13

    - fix port and host accessors, change check now use "==" and not "is".

0.1.3 2017-09-29

    - setup now use setuptools.

0.1.2 2017-09-28

    - fix 'Rx' label on error.
    - change file mode for server.py example.
    - fix compatibility with modbus unit_id = 0 (thanks to mfkenney).
    - fix compatibility for modbus frame with garbage.

0.1.1 2016-05-30

    - add toggle_bit() to utils.
    - add server.py example.
    - add HOWTO for safe PyPI upload.

0.1.0 2016-05-30

    - fix some issues in PEP 8 conformance and inline doc.
    - client modbus RTU: move crc16 compute to utils.
    - add write_multiple_coils() function (code 0x0f).
    - add test_bit(), set_bit(), reset_bit() to utils.
    - add a modbus/TCP multithreaded server through ModbusServer class (for test only).

0.0.13 2015-12-24

    - add auto_open and auto_close to README.rst and quickstart doc.
    - add example min_read_bit.py for show minimal code approach.

0.0.12 2015-12-11

    - add auto_open and auto_close mode to ModbusClient.
    - add accessor function for socket timeout.
    - close TCP socket if hostname change
    - close TCP socket if port change

0.0.11 2015-03-27

    - fix sock.settimeout missing (thanks to bonaime).
    - fix PEP 8 style (thanks to bonaime).

0.0.10 2015-01-22

    - Add timeout parameter to ModbusClient constructor (thanks to bonaime).

0.0.9 2014-10-10

    - Fix rx_byte_count check in ModbusClient class.

0.0.8 2014-09-23

    - Catch excepts on socket send/recv.
    - Sphinx documentation include a quickstart and examples.

0.0.7 2014-08-31

    - Add unit test (see test/).
    - Add params host/port/unit_id/debug on ModbusClient constructor.
    - Add utils module for modbus data mangling.

0.0.6 2014-08-25

    - Fix "socket error" message when call open() on dual stack IPv6/4 host.
    - Check rx byte count field in functions 1 to 4.
    - Fix max bit number problem in functions 1 and 2 (from 125 to 2000).
    - Add debug message, if _send() call on close socket.
    - Rename module name from const to constants.
    - Update MANIFEST.in to remove docs and examples from sdist archive.
    - Update README.rst sample code for Python3.

0.0.5 2014-08-08

    - Now deal with IPv6 host.
    - Fix Python3 issue in _crc().
    - Improve modbus RTU receive code.
    - Secure frame size before struct.unpack invocation.

0.0.4 2014-08-07

    - Add class documentation (add doc/ and sphinx/ directory).
    - Add sphinx docstring in client.py.

0.0.3 2014-08-05

    - Fix padding problem in write_single_coil().
    - Add new examples.

0.0.2 2014-08-05

    - Compatibility with Python 3 and 2.7.
    - Use RST format for README instead of markdown, now set long_description.
    - Add a MANIFEST.in file and include examples/ on sdist.

0.0.1 2014-08-04

    - First release of pyModbusTCP.
